w: 1.~Praise to the Lord, the Al- might- y, the King of cre- a- tion! 
w: 2.~Praise to the Lord, Who o'er all things so won- drous- ly reign- eth, 
w: 3.~Praise to the Lord, Who hath fear- ful- ly, won- drous- ly, made thee; 
w: 4.~Praise to the Lord, Who doth pros- per thy work and de- fend thee; 
w: 5.~Praise to the Lord, Who, when tem- pests their war- fare are wa- ging, 
w: 6.~Praise to the Lord, Who, when dark- ness of sin is a- bound- ing,
w: 7.~Praise to the Lord, O let all that is in me a- dore Him!
